From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Phononenom <64574232+Phononenom@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 12:44:59 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: the session's start takes
 Playtendoh's settings

headless/main.cpp: anti-aliasing, FSR sharpening and the speed limit at each start; Performance > Memory as
the core's switches (texture memory, when memory runs short, keep loaded shaders, memory packing), each set
only where env.txt has not (a line in env.txt wins); the AV1 decoder's threads and frame delay; the
console's defaults for the core's switches.

From these commits (oldest first):
- 2026-11-18 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: task and mesh draws take Lichii's fallback by default
- 2026-11-18 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: Lichii's built-in game patches apply without a mods folder
- 2026-11-20 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: the give-back runs between the GPU back thread's entries (core 0117)
- 2026-11-20 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: refused memory waits before the session ends
- 2026-11-22 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: GPU threads wait on a refused heap allocation, and waits free memory
- 2026-11-23 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: its anti-aliasing, FSR sharpening and speed limit at each start
- 2026-11-23 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: Settings > Performance > Memory as the core's switches
